      "at": "2026-08-11 13:40 UTC",
      "source_author": "FabrizioRomano",
      "source": "\ud83d\udea8\ud83d\udd34\ud83d\udd35 Paris Saint-Germain agree deal in principle with Parma to sign Zion Suzuki, here we go!\n\nJapanese goalkeeper joins for the future at fee worth \u20ac35m package. \ud83c\uddef\ud83c\uddf5\n\nPSG consider loan for Suzuki to play regularly, Juventus will make a decision soon as top candidates. \u26aa\ufe0f\u26ab\ufe0f https://t.co/b5f0Lstn4M",
      "post": "BREAKING: PSG agree \u20ac35m deal for Japanese goalkeeper Zion Suzuki.\n\nThen immediately loan him out because they've bought a goalkeeper they don't need yet. Very PSG.",
      "x_url": "https://x.com/ItsOnlyAGamee/status/2087172255134712147",
      "threads_url": null
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-11 14:44 UTC",
      "source_author": "FabrizioRomano",
      "source": "\ud83d\udea8\ud83c\uddf8\ud83c\uddf3 Understand Iliman Ndiaye has decided not to proceed with Al Hilal deal: he wants to stay in Premier League.\n\nNo to Saudi Arabia move despite big money on the table; Everton winger wants to continue in Premier League, decision made. https://t.co/uVd6p49v7F",
      "post": "BREAKING: Iliman Ndiaye turns down Al Hilal's massive Saudi money to stay at Everton.\n\nEverton fans wondering if he's checked their league position lately or if the PL contract just comes with free therapy.",
      "x_url": "https://x.com/ItsOnlyAGamee/status/2087188338264752315",
      "threads_url": null
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-11 15:11 UTC",
      "source_author": "FabrizioRomano",
      "source": "\ud83d\udea8\ud83d\udd34\u26aa\ufe0f Verbal agreement in place between Sheffield United and Manchester City for new loan deal for Kalvin Phillips.\n\nAll set for the move, waiting on medical as @dannyhall04 reports. https://t.co/w1kbXxKhXC",
      "post": "BREAKING: Kalvin Phillips loaned out again.\n\nCity have now spent enough on Phillips to buy a decent midfielder. Instead they're renting him to Sheffield United like a Netflix subscription they forgot to cancel.",
      "x_url": "https://x.com/ItsOnlyAGamee/status/2087195080713212302",
      "threads_url": null
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-11 18:11 UTC",
      "source_author": "henrywinter",
      "source": "Increasing focus on JP Morgan role in Gianni Infantino\u2019s hastily-abandoned plan to sell off parts of the World Cup. Bankers now getting scrutiny, the latest inspection in the Telegraph today. It\u2019s obviously all about the money for them but surely somebody involved in the process might have mentioned what the inevitable reaction and outcome would be. Humiliation. \n\nSurely somebody had even the faintest knowledge of football, and the emotion it stirs, and that they were not simply toying with a struggling soybean operation somewhere in the Midwest. They were toying with the world\u2019s game, the World Cup. And billions care.  \n\nA financial institution staffed with some very intelligent people must have remembered its involvement in the European Super League fiasco. Humiliation. \u201cWe clearly misjudged how this deal would be viewed by the wider football community and how it might affect them in the future,\u201d a JP Morgan spokesperson said back in 2021. \u201cWe will learn from this.\u201d Clearly not. Next to their  boardroom they need a readtheroom.",
      "post": "JP Morgan backing Infantino's World Cup sell-off plan, getting exposed in the Telegraph.\n\nThese are the same geniuses who funded the Super League three years ago. \"We will learn from this\" they said. Clearly they've learned absolutely nothing.",
      "x_url": "https://x.com/ItsOnlyAGamee/status/2087240571173904872",
      "threads_url": null
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-11 19:50 UTC",
      "source_author": "FabrizioRomano",
      "source": "\ud83d\udea8\ud83c\udde6\ud83c\uddf7 Enzo Maresca would love to reunite with Enzo Fern\u00e1ndez at Manchester City since the start of the window.\n\nThis was the case even before Rodri talks with Bar\u00e7a.\n\nDeal depends on price: Chelsea insist on \u00a3120m fee; #CFC would be happy to welcome Enzo back and keep him. https://t.co/OJzAcjXYy1",
      "post": "BREAKING: Enzo Maresca wants to reunite with Enzo Fern\u00e1ndez at Man City.\n\nChelsea demanding \u00a3120m. So they're pricing him out of a move to their former manager's new club. Classic.",
      "x_url": "https://x.com/ItsOnlyAGamee/status/2087265278426280292",
      "threads_url": null
    },
    {
      "at": "2026-08-11 20:07 UTC",
      "source_author": "FabrizioRomano",
